WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.667
There is

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.868
new CNN reporting

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.802
about the military

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.870
that we want to bring you.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.771
It's about the U.S.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.272
Army's air defense units.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.073
They are among

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.309
the most overworked in the military.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.977
They've been stretched thin

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.579
by global threats.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.313
The critical Army

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.181
defense units are tasked with providing

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.049
a round the clock

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.417
deterrence against our country's

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.185
biggest adversaries.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.854
CNN national security producer

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.389
Haley Brisket joins us now

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.224
from Washington with more.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:24.657
Haley,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.959
tell us what you discovered

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.428
and what you're hearing from folks inside

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.397
the armed services.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.732
Yeah, so Boris, like you

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.600
said, the Army Air

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.101
Defense Branch is one of,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.170
if not the most deployed

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.105
branches in the service as senior

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.873
leaders are saying

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.775
that they have been deploying

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.743
to the Pacific, to the Middle East

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.377
and to Europe.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:44.744
Of course,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.311
as we see them

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.413
trading up Ukrainians

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.914
to provide their own air defense

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.582
against Russia's invasion

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:49.949
and those are

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.017
critically important missions,

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.519
but they are having an impact

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.386
on soldiers.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:53.953
Leaders say

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.588
that they're seeing an increase

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.023
in air defense, soldiers seeking out

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:57.724
behavioral health.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.691
So meaning

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.826
trying to go get mental health

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.494
support on post.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.263
They're also concerned of the wear

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.664
and tear that these deployments

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.865
are having on families.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.934
And while the unpredictable nature

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.269
of these deployments

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.071
so leaders are working hard

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:11.704
to mitigate

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.906
some of that pressure to take on

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.007
some of the pressure on soldiers,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.542
because really those demands around

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.077
the world are only increasing

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.278
and will only be increasing

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.979
over the next several years.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.314
And in some regions,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.550
that threat is specifically

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.684
looming large.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.186
Where are those regions

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:26.986
where these units are

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.288
feeling the hardest strain

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.490
So the

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.458
Indo-Pacific and

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:31.991
Europe are where

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.326
we're seeing some major strain

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.494
on these units right now

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.528
in the Indo-Pacific,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.963
these soldiers are not only dealing

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.198
with a lengthy list

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.365
of operational requirements,

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.267
but also training exercises

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.702
with foreign allies and partners

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:43.436
in the region.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.370
And given the vast

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.473
size of the Indo-Pacific,

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:47.173
they are

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.142
taking multiple days away from family

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.543
just to travel, let alone

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.212
do the exercises themselves.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:52.912
And then, of course,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.781
we have the soldiers in Europe

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.448
who are now training

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.716
Ukrainians on their own air

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.450
defense systems,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.519
provided by the US and their allies.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.689
And so we I spoke with a U.S.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.423
soldier who helped

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.557
head up that Patriot

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.625
training for the Ukrainians,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.759
who said it was some of the most

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.560
grueling

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.595
training days he's had,

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.897
just given how intense they are, knowing

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.532
what is at stake here

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.100
and hoping to give these Ukrainians

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.668
every possible chance

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.736
and giving them every tool

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.005
in their toolkit on air defense

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.707
and how our military leaders

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.342
trying to address the problem now.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:24.477
Yeah.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.745
So multiple lines of effort

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.880
here, Boris, by the Army.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.780
We have

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.450
that's quite big enlistment bonus.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.518
The Army is now offering

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.252
for some air

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:35.054
defense jobs a little over $47,000

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.623
and hoping to fill out

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.024
some of these new air defense units

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.958
and they'll be standing up

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.560
over the next several years.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.661
They also are embedding

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:42.762
mental health specialists

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.897
into the brigades

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.398
in order to give these soldiers

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.200
someone to talk to if they need it.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.068
Reducing commitment in the Middle East,

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.403
going from five battalions

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.271
deploying in that region

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.173
to two battalions now

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.073
because partners are able

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.909
to kind of provide their own air defense.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.610
And then also just encouraging leaders

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.012
to increase their communication

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.313
with families, mitigate

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.714
some of that pressure

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.849
and that unpredictability.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.951
So leaders are really working

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.785
in the background here

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.220
to try to take care of their soldiers

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.522
while also meeting those mounting

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.557
mission requirements.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.191
And joining me

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.992
now is CNN military analyst

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.027
and retired U.S.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:14.928
Army commanding

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.829
general Mark Hertling

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.865
for some reaction to that story.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.432
Now, General,

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.234
what do you make of the Army's

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.536
concerns about this rampant burnout

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.138
among its missile defense units?

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:25.772
I mean, this is something

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.207
that's always been a problem.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.810
Paula, this is not new.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.445
Hailey's reporting is very good,

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.279
but it's a problem

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.281
that's been around for decades.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.517
It has to do with the type of equipment

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.518
we're talking about.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.620
Air defense falls into three categories

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.756
manned, portable, the ones that are fired

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.258
from a soldier

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.393
shoulder like the Stinger missile.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.195
Something they call

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.664
Nomad, which is the low

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.366
altitude equipment.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.534
Like they get parts

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.301
or that

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.070
The Avengers

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.972
that we're seeing in Ukraine right now.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:03:59.973
And then there's the high

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.941
that the high altitude equipment

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.676
that shoots down cruise missiles,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.611
ballistic missiles,

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:06.045
and high flying aircraft.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.680
It's the high in that area

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.082
where there are the problems,

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.184
the so-called Patriot systems.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.052
And it's very easy for the public to say,

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.887
hey, let's just send the Patriots here

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.555
or send them there.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.956
But there are very few

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.957
of these equipment.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.093
They're called high demand,

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.362
low density pieces of equipment.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.197
There's several areas in the Army

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.031
that are like this.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.533
And Patriot is the number one system

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.301
that's like this.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.535
And it's because, number one,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.737
they cost so much.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.337
Number two,

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.473
it takes so much time to train

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.574
soldiers on them.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.775
And number three,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.710
they have defensive requirements

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.879
in various parts of the world.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.815
As Haley mentioned, Korea, Taiwan,

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.317
the Middle East.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.985
And we've been supporting our

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.553
our allies and partners

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.189
with some of these systems as well.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.591
I want to read you something

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.191
that the commander

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:52.659
of the 10th

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.526
Army Air and missile

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.296
Defense Command said in Europe, quote,

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.532
Unfortunately, business is good for air

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.066
defense.

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:00.867
Of course,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.168
that's very apparent

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.469
when it comes to Ukraine.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:06.039
So do you think this burnout could impact

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:07.206
or even threaten the

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.641
US's efforts in Ukraine?

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.145
Oh, certainly could.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.147
And the 10th air and missile defense

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:14.614
command in

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.249
Europe used to be one of the units

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.583
I commanded in Europe.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.919
There was one Patriot battalion

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:20.953
a unit

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.056
that has three batteries of Patriot.

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.457
We have given

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.626
one of those batteries to Ukraine.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.095
So it is down now to two batteries

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.065
with with about 90 soldiers in Iraq.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.232
What happens is

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.267
when you give those

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.802
pieces of equipment away

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.870
or when you send them off to allies,

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.472
the soldiers that remain

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.540
that are still doing

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.507
a very viable

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.775
mission are stuck

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.976
with taking up the slack.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.412
It's like taking an entire organization,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.880
cutting it by a third,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.981
and then saying, hey,

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.550
continue to do the mission

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.851
you've been asked to do.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:52.819
That's what's happening.

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:55.288
So the tent embassy in Europe

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.956
is just one of several

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.990
that are like this.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:58.758
And yeah,

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.259
they work is good,

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.161
but there's not that many of them.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.296
And the next question

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:04.530
I'm sure you're going to ask,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.131
well, well,

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:07.333
why didn't the Army make more of these?

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.602
Because they are extremely expensive.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.671
And there's a budget that has to do with

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.606
not only the systems,

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.475
but also the missiles that they fire.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.210
Fair enough.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.277
Now, speaking of Ukraine, though,

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.179
the country's deputy defense minister

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:20.780
just announced

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.348
that Russian forces

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.917
have made advances in eastern Ukraine.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.286
How significant is this

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.257
Well, all the rage that I'm getting,

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.525
Paul, is the fact that

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.127
that Ukrainian forces

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:35.528
are actually countering

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.330
those Russian advances

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.499
in the eastern part in the Donbas.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:40.500
And at the same time,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.734
the Ukrainian forces

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.836
are also continuing their efforts

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.972
in the southeastern part of the country,

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.507
that region herself.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:50.643
So all of the front lines, that 600 mile

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.511
or 600

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.045
kilometer of front line

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:53.780
from the north

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:54.514
all the way down to

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.649
the southeast is being covered.

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:59.519
Ukraine is advancing in many of them.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.354
Russia is taking advantage

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:04.257
and attempting to regain some territory.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.825
But every read that I'm getting

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:07.593
from my counterparts in Ukraine

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.761
is that they're not being

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.029
very successful in doing.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.999
Also overnight, Russia launched

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.767
an air attack on the capital of Kiev.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.870
The city's military administration says

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.907
that Russia used Iranian made drones.

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:21.541
Kiev's air

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.743
defenses destroyed all of the drones,

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.344
according to the city's leaders.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.913
But multiple homes were damaged

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.381
by falling debris.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.049
A resident was injured.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:32.084
Is this a growing threat for Ukraine?

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:32.685
I mean, Russia

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:36.122
using these Iranian drones?

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:38.291
It's been a threat for six months.

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.826
The combination of drones,

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:40.793
which are relatively

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.829
cheap, are sent in first.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.730
So it drains off some of the air

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.065
defense pieces of equipment.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.433
We were just talking about.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.268
And then they send in the Russians will

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.471
then send in the larger missiles

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:54.707
after they think they've depleted

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.509
weapons against the drones.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.277
So you're going to see this combination

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.379
tactics of of firing

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.950
actually very inexpensive drones

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:05.051
against cities

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:07.286
that have large explosive power

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:09.722
to drain off the Ukrainian air defense.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:10.890
And then followed up

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.391
by much bigger missiles.

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:13.292
And that's part of the air

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:13.993
defense problem

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.561
we were talking about earlier.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.730
The amount of weapons

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.899
that are being used to counter this

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:20.800
air threat

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.935
by Russia is just off the chart.

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.771
We have never seen this many drones.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.373
This many fire

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:29.775
caliber missiles fired at one time.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.377
And the good news is

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.713
Ukraine is shooting down most of them.

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.982
They they've put up a protective barrier

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.450
a wall, if you will.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.918
It's very difficult to do.

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:40.553
And they're having more success

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.888
than countries like Israel

00:08:41.888 --> 00:08:43.322
using the Iron Dome.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:45.091
They are actually protecting their people

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:45.992
very well.

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.159
With the equipment

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.995
they've been given by the West.

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:51.230
But again, we get back to the problem,

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.298
low density,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.633
high demand equipment

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.501
being used in Ukraine

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:56.736
that have been purchased

00:08:56.736 --> 00:08:58.638
truthfully for our security, for the U.S.

00:08:58.638 --> 00:08:59.071
security.

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:00.873
General Mark

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.975
Hertling, thank you

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:04.744
Pleasure, Paula.

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:05.144
Thank you.

